Hi Phil,

I tried to download the dev version of mirt using the instructions on your GitHub. I had version 1.29 and when I downloaded from GitHub, it updated to 1.29.8 (versus dev version 1.30). I’m not sure if I didn something wrong— but any advice on how to obtain dev version 1.30? Downloading using devtools didn’t work the first time so I used the Mac OSX instructions you have on your GitHub that instructs to download manually via terminal. Then I went back into R and used devtools (install_github('philchalmers/mirt'))to install and it was able to download an updated package but was not version 1.30.  After downloading, I used the C2 stat in the M2 function, and I’m getting negative CFI/TLI values so know my update is not correct.. thanks so much,

Keri

