Message-ID: <DHGI0frHJUI.KILPKxf7AgAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <DHGI0frHJUI.s2DFPNolAgAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
References: <DHGI0frHJUI.Udy9eMRtAAAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com> <DHGI0frHJUI.s2DFPNolAgAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/DHGI0frHJUI/m/KILPKxf7AgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If the IRT model estimated is exploratory this behavior is expected. The models are rotationally indeterminate, so negative loadings will occur in the usual geometry. Confirmatory models are less likely to have these negative loadings, but they still are possible due to the fact that these are often partial coefficeints when items have more than one loading/slope.

Phil

