From ub330c2028fed415b at groups.google.com  Fri Dec  7 17:19:32 2018
From: ub330c2028fed415b at groups.google.com (Phil Chalmers)
Date: Fri, 07 Dec 2018 17:19:32 +0000
Subject: Re: cross-validation fit
Message-ID: <94ikLpmNM8I.tJ3NNkv7AgAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <94ikLpmNM8I.GUWLkk8uAgAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
References: <94ikLpmNM8I._FSQV2kQBgAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com> <94ikLpmNM8I.GUWLkk8uAgAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/94ikLpmNM8I/m/tJ3NNkv7AgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Because M2 computes the collapsed moments based on the orthogonal compliment of the freely estimated parameters. Hence, you can't use the pars$est <- FALSE approach, because it's computing the M2 statistic based on parameters you are assuming to be fixed and known a priori. Other stats may not be this limited, but for the M2 you'd have to leave these parameters as estimated (i.e., your fit2).

Phil

